okay welcome back everyone so uh now  that we understand how to build a  cryptocurrency from a blockchain uh  let's see how to manage those  cryptocurrencies in what we call a  crypto wallet okay so how do we use  cryptocurrencies in the real world so  just a quick review to remind you as we  said as we looked at the blockchain  network basically um the balance of  bitcoins that i own is basically is held  in these unspent transaction outputs  that correspond to addresses that belong  to me what does belong to me mean belong  to me means that i have the secret key  that corresponds to the public key of  those addresses  now other blockchains actually don't use  the utxo model for example the ethereum  blockchain  actually has accounts where every  account  holds a value so i have again it's all  based on signatures so my i have an  account that corresponds to a public key  and a secret key but there's a value  associated with that with that account  written um on the blockchain and when i  want to spend funds i i sign a  transaction that subtracts or add funds  to the uh amounts available in the  account so it's not a collection of  utxos but rather explicit accounting  of how much money every address has yeah  so every address as we say has an  associated value and a transaction just  moves values between um between  addresses so these are kind of different  ways of representing  data on the blockchain you know either  accounts or utxos it turns out utxos  require less memory on the part of the  miners but um  but are less flexible than accounts so  for example with an account system you  could just look on the blockchain and  immediately know how much value is  associated with a particular address in  the utxo model to figure out how much  value is associated with an address you  have to go and sum up all the values of  across all utxos in the blockchains that  correspond to that address yeah so there  are trade-offs between these two ways to  represent value different blockchains as  you can see do it do it differently but  for our discussion in this segment  that's not so relevant i want to talk  about how to actually manage um those  crypto assets once you buy them okay so  just to be clear uh the crypto assets  themselves are secret are represented as  secret keys that allows you allow you to  sign transactions the question is where  do you store those secret keys and how  do you use those secret keys okay so we  do that using what we call a wallet and  what is a wallet well a wallet is  basically some client-side software that  allows us helps us manage our assets  okay so what does a wallet do well you  know it stores all of my secret signing  keys and when i want to spend  transactions when i want to spend funds  or receive funds basically um the wallet  allows me to spend funds and it also  confirms when someone send sends  funds to me  so a typical example wallet let's say  for the ethereum network is a wallet  called metamask this is kind of a fun  pro a fun system to play with i actually  suggest  download download it as a chrome  extension it's an extension that sits  inside of you inside of your browser it  basically manages um your crypto assets  and allows you to receive funds and send  funds from your address we'll see how in  just a minute so here's an example of  the user interface uh for meta mask once  you install an installer on your system  basically there's an address associated  um with this uh with this uh particular  wallet in fact you can have multiple  addresses associated with a wallet  here's one particular address that  address currently  holds one each so one if currently is a  couple hundred dollars um and the secret  keys that are needed to spend from that  from that address right remember the  secret keys are used to sign  transactions to spend funds from those  address those secret keys are basically  held on my clients so my machine  basically holds the secret keys and i  can tell metamask go ahead and send  funds somewhere and metamask will use  those secret keys to sign a transaction  to send the funds
 

